		"targetLanguageCode": "fr-FR",
		"introImage": {
			"src": "img/lo7/opinions-matter.svg",
			"alt": "Opinions matter illustration"
		},
		"introHTML": "<p>This lesson teaches learners how to express likes, dislikes, and preferences in French using verbs such as <em>aimer</em>, <em>adorer</em>, <em>détester</em>, and <em>préférer</em>. It introduces sentence patterns for talking about activities, sports, and favourite things, and shows how to use definite articles with general nouns (for example <em>j&apos;aime le football</em>, <em>je n&apos;aime pas la natation</em>). Learners also practise interrogative adjectives (<em>quel</em>, <em>quelle</em>, <em>quels</em>, <em>quelles</em>) to ask questions, and work on pronunciation of borrowed English words like <em>le tennis</em>, <em>le foot</em>, and <em>le week-end</em>.</p>",
		"informationHTML": "<h3>After completing this unit, you will be able to:</h3><ul><li>Talk about likes, dislikes, and preferences in French.</li><li>Use common verbs such as <em>aimer</em>, <em>adorer</em>, <em>détester</em>, and <em>préférer</em> with greater confidence.</li><li>Use definite articles more accurately when talking about sports, activities, and general things.</li><li>Ask and answer questions about favourite activities, colours, and countries.</li><li>Recognise how some borrowed English words are pronounced in French.</li></ul>"
	},
